WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.430
- I'm in El Paso, Texas

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.530
outside the Sacred Heart Catholic Church

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.660
just across the border from Ciudad Juarez.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.590
Officials here in El Paso
estimate as many as 2,500 people

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.800
have built an encampment in
and around this neighborhood,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.533
primarily around this
church seeking refuge.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.003
(Luz Maria speaks Spanish)

00:00:28.482 --> 00:00:30.899
(soft music)

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.560
The migrant population has surged

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.740
in advance of the end of Title
42, the public health law

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.140
that has allowed the Trump administration

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.670
and now the Biden administration

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.620
to quickly expel many migrants

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.240
who have crossed the border illegally

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.030
before they can ask for
protections in the U.S.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.010
Some of these migrants, an untold number,

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.410
actually crossed the
border without encountering

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.820
federal immigration officials

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.803
and are without papers at this point.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.880
- I am declaring a state of
emergency in our community.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.290
And the reason why we're declaring

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.230
a state of emergency is to
make sure that we can stand up

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.650
and be prepared for May 11th, May 12th

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.920
to have public sheltering, public housing.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.870
- Rumors are rampant across the border

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.450
in Ciudad Juarez, according
to local officials here,

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.040
that if you can make it to the U.S.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.860
by the 11th, you'll be fine.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.420
That's not accurate.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.980
Migrants without documentation

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.690
won't be able to leave the city,

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.550
and those encountered by the border patrol

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.620
still are subject as Title 42.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.710
And after the 11th, many
will face swift removal

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.640
if they're not eligible

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.300
for asylum processes here in the U.S.

00:01:39.803 --> 00:01:43.220
(Aracely speaks Spanish)

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.440
Once Title 42 does expire, the
U.S. government will go back

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.510
to processing people
under its normal order,

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.160
what's called Title 8.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.870
With that comes swift removal

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.270
for those who don't qualify for asylum

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.010
and the possibility of bans

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.680
on returning to the United
States for up to five years,

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.103
and criminal charges, a
felony, if folks do come back.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.820
This latest surge of migrants
here in the city of El Paso

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.650
mirrors one experienced in December,

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.530
the last time Title 42 was set to expire.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.120
The difference now,
local officials tell me,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.740
is there's more people.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:32.850
- We figure that it's anywhere
between 10 to 12,000 people

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.750
that are ready to come
on May 11th, May 12th.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.873
We do know that there's additional
coming right behind them.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.180
- Right now, in the background

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.470
across the city of El Paso,

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.380
officials are building
out shelter capacity.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.870
They're preparing a pair
of decommissioned schools

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.020
to eventually house several
hundred if not more migrants

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.721
expected in the area in the coming days.

00:02:54.721 --> 00:02:57.138
(soft music)

